This GUI app will allow to generate, customize and play backing tracks starting
from a single audio file.

These are the features to implement:
- via a free LLM model the input audio is separated into several tracks, ideally
  one for each instrument or voice;
- the tracks will be shown (via their waveforms) from top to bottom, the x-axis
  is the time and is shared between the tracks;
- each track will have a Mute and a Solo button, to set if it plays or not;
- the user can play and listen to only the tracks they set for playing;
- the user can jump to any point in the song with a mouse click;
- the user can set a loop for playing setting two loop points in the timeline;
- the user can choose to transpose the tracks by an integer number of semitones
  (negative values included);
- the user can slow down or speed up the tempo of the tracks (without changing
  their pitch);
- the user can save the single tracks and the current settings as a project;
- the user can render the current audible tracks to a single audio file;

Future features:
- an extra track will be put at the top with a generated metronome beat (this
  implies the autodetection of the tempo throughout the song);
- the user can add an intro count before the beginning of the song (this also
  implies the autodetection of the BPMs at the start);
